<p>Postgres 17 is out today, and we’re here for it. In keeping with our <a href="https://neon.tech/docs/postgresql/postgres-version-policy#major-versions">version policy</a>, the latest major version is now available for all Neon users including those on the Free plan. <a href="https://console.neon.tech/signup">Get your Postgres 17 database</a> and start exploring the latest features immediately.</p>
<h2 id="how-to-speed-run-postgres-17-on-neon" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>How to speed run Postgres 17 on Neon</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#how-to-speed-run-postgres-17-on-neon" aria-label="Link to How to speed run Postgres 17 on Neon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2>
<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> <a href="https://console.neon.tech/signup">Create a Neon account</a>. We only need your login info (no credit card).</p>
<p><span aria-owns="rmiz-modal-" data-rmiz=""><span data-rmiz-content="not-found" style="visibility:visible"><img src="https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/postgres-17/ad4nxeamf1e3ebpiuo30th3bxd1nkqfrvpmdlxy7csfmntanstsisxvpislaiq-z8jid3s0edifduebbffvmxylsqpma6evbwzigzfazptqc1qubwkx9l-ydvgncbjz04knenvrt9kqgdp3sfhhjx3srfxspyyy-55e8923e.png" alt="Image"/></span></span></p>
<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Select <code>Postgres 17</code> for your project</p>
<p><span aria-owns="rmiz-modal-" data-rmiz=""><span data-rmiz-content="not-found" style="visibility:visible"><img src="https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/postgres-17/screenshot-2024-09-26-at-62709percente2percent80percentafam-1-856x1024-81f5f76a.png" alt="Image"/></span></span></p>
<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> That’s it. Your Postgres 17 database is already up and running. You can start querying directly from the <a href="https://neon.tech/docs/get-started-with-neon/query-with-neon-sql-editor">Neon SQL Editor</a> or <a href="https://neon.tech/docs/connect/query-with-psql-editor">connecting with psql.</a></p>
<p><span aria-owns="rmiz-modal-" data-rmiz=""><span data-rmiz-content="not-found" style="visibility:visible"><img src="https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/postgres-17/ad4nxcctdsltbzsajw4mvcnjo7q0d4r3ilk2c2sxtdlg72aduyru8ih2d73pszinbkw9jddtg2dqospl07q615ndokpxwiw53zjf6ogxaafkuc8iwwrin7hn1bctossro-2yoevpkk5ruf8h6vmqcvmraa-8778685f.png" alt="Image"/></span></span></p>
