<p>Use the MERGE command with RETURNING:</p>
<figure class="code-block group/code-block relative flex flex-col [&amp;_pre]:min-w-full" data-has-filename="false"><pre class="shiki css-variables" style="background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)" tabindex="0" data-language="sql"><code class="grid"><span class="line" data-line="1"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">MERGE</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)"> INTO</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)"> heroes </span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">AS</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)"> h</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="2"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">USING</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)"> (</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">VALUES</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)"> (</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string-expression)">&#x27;Wade&#x27;</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">, </span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string-expression)">&#x27;Wilson&#x27;</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">, </span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string-expression)">&#x27;Deadpool&#x27;</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">)) </span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">AS</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)"> v(first_name, last_name, hero_name)</span></span>
